The screen to allow user to create voucher posting. 

Remarks – screen to allow user to input either a common remark for the entire batch or separate remarks against each voucher entry. Remarks will be alpha-numeric only. 

Schedule execution time – This is an optional input. The user can propose a preferred voucher execution time by setting a specific date and time. When all approvals are complete the system will check if a schedule is provided. If it’s provided it will execute the posting only on or after the scheduled time. Posting will not occur before the scheduled time.  If no time is specified, the vouchers will be posted immediately upon final approval. In case if the schedule time lapsed the Last approver will be prompted about the same, user can decide either it can be allowed to execute immediately or can be scheduled. 

Branch – Branch code entered by the user, will be searched in the database and only available branch can be selected for voucher posting. This is a mandatory field. 

Currency – User must choose currency from the dropdown. This is a mandatory field. 

CGL - CGL code entered by the user, will be searched in the database and only available CGL can be selected for voucher posting. This is a mandatory field. 

Amount - This is a mandatory field. The maximum allowed value is 9999999999999999.9999. No negative value is allowed. 

Type – User must select either Debit or Credit for every voucher entry. 

Product Code – This is an optional field; user can add numeric product code up to 8 digits. 

Add row – allows user to add the voucher row. 

Delete row– Will delete the voucher row. 

Submit – All the voucher entries will be validated with as per business validations. User can submit the voucher batch only if all the validations are satisfied. 

